                <pb facs="0651" n="555" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg555"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/206: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Thurston</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-08-23T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 23,
                                1921—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>39. Department informed that during the last week Nicaraguan Government has had
                    strong suspicions that a concerted movement was on foot to cause an uprising
                    there. … Department informed further that a telegram of warning was sent by the
                    Government of Costa Rica to the President of Nicaragua stating that a
                    revolutionary band of about 80 men were preparing to invade Nicaragua from Costa
                    Rica. Nicaraguan Government is also experiencing trouble with invasion by small
                    body of men from Honduras and has sent military forces to both Honduran and
                    Costa Rican frontiers.</p>
                <p>You will endeavor to verify the statements made above with reference to Costa
                    Rica and report by cable as to whether or not, in your opinion, Costa Rica is
                    taking proper measures to prevent her neutrality being violated.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
